.TH "COMPLYCTL\-PROVIDER\-OPENSCAP" "1" "September 2026" "ComplyTime Manual"
.SH NAME
complyctl\-provider\-openscap \- OpenSCAP scanning provider for
complyctl
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]complyctl\-provider\-openscap\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]complyctl\-provider\-openscap\f[R] is a gRPC plugin for
\f[B]complyctl\f[R](1) that provides compliance scanning capabilities
using the OpenSCAP engine.
It is not invoked directly by users; \f[B]complyctl\f[R] discovers and
launches it automatically when the provider is installed.
.PP
The provider receives assessment configurations from
\f[B]complyctl\f[R], generates XCCDF tailoring files matching the
requested profiles, executes scans via the \f[B]oscap\f[R] command\-line
tool, and returns structured results.
It supports automatic datastream selection via CPE\-based matching
against the host system.
.PP
Communication with \f[B]complyctl\f[R] uses the hashicorp/go\-plugin
gRPC interface, implementing three RPCs: \f[B]Describe\f[R],
\f[B]Generate\f[R], and \f[B]Scan\f[R].
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is provided through variables defined in assessment plan
targets.
These variables are passed to the provider via \f[B]complyctl\f[R] and
are not set manually by the user.
.TP
\f[B]profile\f[R] (required)
XCCDF profile ID to evaluate.
Must match the pattern \f[B][a\-zA\-Z0\-9\-_.]+\f[R].
Examples: \f[B]cis_server_l1\f[R],
\f[B]xccdf_org.ssgproject.content_profile_cis\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]datastream\f[R] (optional)
Absolute path to an SSG XCCDF datastream XML file.
When omitted, the provider auto\-detects the appropriate datastream by
matching the system\(cqs CPE (from the os\-release file) against CPE
metadata embedded in the SSG datastream files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\f[B]SSG_CONTENT_DIR\f[R]
Directory containing SSG datastream XML files.
Used during auto\-detection when \f[B]datastream\f[R] is not specified.
Default: \f[B]/usr/share/xml/scap/ssg/content\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]OS_RELEASE_FILE\f[R]
Path to the os\-release file used for CPE extraction during datastream
auto\-detection.
Default: \f[B]/etc/os\-release\f[R]
.SH EXTERNAL TOOLS
Requires \f[B]oscap\f[R] (provided by the \f[B]openscap\-scanner\f[R]
package) at runtime.
The provider locates \f[B]oscap\f[R] via \f[B]PATH\f[R] lookup.
.PP
The \f[B]scap\-security\-guide\f[R] package provides the SSG datastream
files used for evaluation.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[I].complytime/openscap/\f[R]
Provider workspace directory.
All paths below are relative to the current working directory.
.TP
\f[I].complytime/openscap/policy/tailoring.xml\f[R]
XCCDF tailoring file generated by the \f[B]Generate\f[R] RPC.
Contains the selected profile rules matched from the assessment
configuration.
.TP
\f[I].complytime/openscap/results/arf.xml\f[R]
Asset Reporting Format (ARF) result file produced by \f[B]oscap xccdf
eval \(enresults\-arf\f[R] during the \f[B]Scan\f[R] RPC.
.TP
\f[I].complytime/openscap/results/results.xml\f[R]
XCCDF results XML file produced alongside the ARF file by \f[B]oscap
xccdf eval \(enresults\f[R].
.TP
\f[I].complytime/openscap/remediations/remediation\-script.sh\f[R]
Bash remediation script generated by \f[B]oscap xccdf generate fix\f[R]
during the \f[B]Generate\f[R] RPC.
.TP
\f[I].complytime/openscap/remediations/remediation\-playbook.yml\f[R]
Ansible remediation playbook generated by \f[B]oscap xccdf generate
fix\f[R].
.TP
\f[I].complytime/openscap/remediations/remediation\-blueprint.toml\f[R]
Blueprint remediation file generated by \f[B]oscap xccdf generate
fix\f[R].
.SH EVIDENCE
The provider records an \f[B]Evidence\f[R] entry on each
\f[B]AssessmentLog\f[R] returned by the \f[B]Scan\f[R] RPC:
.TP
\f[B]Type\f[R]
\f[B]ARF\f[R] \(em Asset Reporting Format.
The ARF file aggregates XCCDF results, OVAL definitions, and system
characteristics into a single SCAP\-standard artifact.
.TP
\f[B]Production\f[R]
The ARF file is produced by running \f[B]oscap xccdf eval
\(enresults\-arf\f[R] against the tailoring file and the SSG datastream.
It is written to \f[I].complytime/openscap/results/arf.xml\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]EvaluationLog representation\f[R]
Each assessment log carries an Evidence entry with:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Source.Coordinate\f[R]: absolute path to the ARF file (e.g.,
\f[I].complytime/openscap/results/arf.xml\f[R])
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Source.Digest\f[R]: \f[B]sha256:<hex>\f[R] digest of the ARF file
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Source.ReferenceID\f[R]: \f[B]openscap\-arf\f[R]
.RE
.SH EXIT CODES
This provider is a gRPC subprocess managed by \f[B]complyctl\f[R].
Exit codes follow the hashicorp/go\-plugin protocol and are not
user\-facing.
